<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5">=F0=9F=8C=B1 Ngu=
=E1=BB=93n G=E1=BB=91c &amp; Motivation: From Blocking to Non-blocking Web<=
/h3>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Network Asynchronous Thread evol=
ution represents one of the most transformative developments trong web tech=
nology history. Early web was <strong>document-centric</strong> - pages loa=
ded once, completely, synchronously. Modern web requires <strong>real-time =
data exchange</strong> m=C3=A0 would be impossible v=E1=BB=9Bi blocking net=
work operations.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Historical Progression:<=
/strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>1991-1995</strong>: Sta=
tic HTML documents, no dynamic loading</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>1996</strong>: Java app=
lets introduce client-side network programming (heavy)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>1999</strong>: XMLHttpR=
equest introduced by Microsoft for Outlook Web Access</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>2005</strong>: AJAX pop=
ularized asynchronous web applications</li>
